# A PlayStation 3 DualShock pairs by having the host MAC written into it over
# USB, so the cable plug is the pairing gesture. Run ds3-pair on every DS3 that
# appears on USB: it is idempotent and only restarts bluetoothd when something
# actually changed, so plugging a pad in purely to charge costs nothing.
#
# ATTRS{} walks up to the USB parent, so this matches cable-connected pads only,
# never a pad that is already connected over bluetooth.
#
# The unit name carries %k (the hidraw node) and --collect is set, because a
# fixed name that has once failed blocks every later run with "Unit
# ds3-pair.service was already loaded" and the next pad you plug in is silently
# ignored.
#
# Added 2026-09-22. Undo: rm this file, udevadm control --reload.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="054c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0268", \
  RUN+="/usr/bin/systemd-run --no-block --collect --unit=ds3-pair-%k /usr/local/sbin/ds3-pair"
